<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="3a8b873c">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product contains stakeholder devised prompts for suppliers to describe their skills, experience and solution
    capabilities. In addition, this work product also includes contextual and instructional information to facilitate
    supplier responses. Contextual and instructional information provides suppliers with the appropriate perspective to
    answer stakeholders questions. Questions posed in a Request For Proposal are typically more detailed than those in
    Request For Information submissions. Information suppliers are typically asked to provide include, but is not limited
    to, the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Functional and technical capabilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Support capabilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Implementation planning
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Pricing information
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        References
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="cc9d10cf"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="68b55107">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The amount and specificity of information included in this work product varies from project to project depending on
        various factors such as project needs, confidentiality.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Some organizations may have an established procurement process for engaging suppliers. Consult with stakeholders to
        verify any existing procurement guidelines to follow.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        In some cases, EY involvement in Request for Proposal documentation may be limited to assisting stakeholders
        develop questions to be answered. In others, EY involvement may be asked to help develop company and project
        overview sections as well as response instructions for suppliers to follow.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Independence Considerations
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    For engagements with Channel 1 clients, EY can advise, review and provide observations on management’s package
    selection. EY cannot draft or develop the request, nor administer the package selection process on the
    client&apos;s behalf.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    For engagements with Channel 2 clients, EY can assist management in the development of a package selection, subject to
    management review and approval.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Although generally permitted for Channel 2 engagements, EY cannot interact directly with a supplier who is an audit
    client if EY is involved in assisting the client with the package selection process, other than very limited
    interaction related to information gathering.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="a8ed3ff"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="b44d8c5e">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product is used for the following purposes:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To communicate specific project needs, circumstances and solution requirements necessary for suppliers to propose a
        solution that includes associated costs and implementation plans
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To capture responses in a standardized format that allows stakeholders to objectively compare different supplier
        responses
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="e6ed7bcb"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="4f515cf"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="cf5cee1a">&lt;p&gt;
    Content in this work product typically contains the following sections. The amount of information and level of
    specificity in each section may vary from one project to the next.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Company and project overview
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section typically contains the following content:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Company overview
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Strategic imperatives that briefly describe the procuring company&apos;s strategic objectives and the goals created to
        achieve objectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Project purpose
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confidentiality statement
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li style=&quot;LIST-STYLE-TYPE: none&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
                Contains an explicit statement of expected confidentiality
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
                Provides a non-disclosure agreement, which must be signed by participating suppliers that confidential
                information about the procurer and the request is not shared with unapproved parties
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Response guidelines and instructions
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section typically contains the following content:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        General rules that describe terms of participation, disclaimers, late submission policy, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Timeline of when supplier responses are expected
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Response instructions for suppliers to follow (e.g., respond in-line to the document, on a separate spreadsheet,
        how or if they can include additional information, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Point of contact to address supplier questions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notification process 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
                Describes how the selection process will proceed, and how the participants will be notified
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li type=&quot;circle&quot;&gt;
                Indicates how many firms will be notified for further evaluation
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Stakeholder questions
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        This section is typically populated with stakeholder derived questions for suppliers to answer
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Appendices
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Includes additional schemas, diagrams or charts that will be useful to the participating suppliers
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="a1e92efa">&lt;p&gt;
    Spreadsheets are commonly used to capture responses because they can be easily manipulated to provide a level of
    organization and functionality that allows stakeholders to capture, score and compare all responses quickly and
    efficiently. In essence, the spreadsheet acts as a form for stakeholders to ask questions and for suppliers to fill in
    their responses. For example, a spreadsheet can be arranged with multiple tabs where each tab prompts suppliers to
    describe different aspects of their company and package capabilities. The responses across all the spreadsheet tabs can
    be formulated to derive a consolidated score.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
